## Summary

I've successfully created the GhostLedger user interface with three files:

### **Files Created**
- **index.html** (5.9 KB) — Semantic HTML with all 29 required element IDs in correct order
- **styles.css** (13 KB) — Dark haunted theme, responsive, print-friendly, no external resources
- **app.js** (25 KB) — State management, UI rendering, localStorage persistence, no network calls

### **Verification Results**

**✓ All Required Element IDs Present**  
Confirmed all 29 IDs in order: dropzone, choose-file, file-input, load-sample, currency, import-report, stat-income, stat-income-sub, stat-spending, stat-spending-sub, stat-net, stat-net-sub, stat-ghosts, stat-ghosts-sub, savings-banner, ghost-list, trend-chart, trend-table, category-bars, budget-list, anomaly-list, txn-search, txn-category, txn-sort, txn-count, txn-body, export-csv, export-json, clear-data

**✓ Zero Network Calls**  
- `grep fetch(` in app.js and engine.js: **0 matches**
- `grep XMLHttpRequest` in app.js and engine.js: **0 matches**

**✓ Syntax Validation**  
- `node --check engine.js` ... OK
- `node --check app.js` ... OK

**✓ Test Suite: All 61 Tests Pass**  
Including subscription detection (11 recurring charges found), sample data import (180 transactions, totals balance exactly), and all amountCents are integers

### **Key Features**
- Import flow with drag-and-drop, file picker, and embedded sample data
- Dashboard with income/spending/net stats and recurring charges
- Ghost subscription cards with exorcise/restore, price hike detection, and yearly savings calculation
- Monthly trend chart (canvas) with text table fallback
- Category spending breakdown and editable monthly budgets
- Searchable/filterable/sortable transactions table with per-transaction category overrides
- Anomaly detection (duplicates, unusual transactions)
- CSV/JSON export and clear-all-data with confirmation
- Full offline operation, 100% privacy, localStorage persistence
- Dark spooky theme with proper accessibility (focus rings, contrast >= AA)
